{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run a background worker on node1 as the dedicated unprivileged account inventorysvc, managed as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system account has UID/GID 999 and a non-login shell. The enabled systemd service was directly observed active with its worker and child process running as UID/GID 999, without capabilities, and producing heartbeat data. It also returned active after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9757deb52c374d2a","cmd-9dd5f9d6f80c42dc","cmd-6fbba0a5948448b6","cmd-82da0ed96b504f89"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Confine the worker's filesystem view to a root-owned chroot, with /var/lib/inventory as its only writable application directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live process root was /srv/inventory-chroot and its working directory was the chroot's /var/lib/inventory. A complete ownership/permission audit found all files and directories outside that subtree root-owned and not group/other-writable. Runtime probes as inventorysvc were denied in representative directories outside the data subtree and succeeded only in /var/lib/inventory. The confinement and write boundary remained intact after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ad9f2432c7be4a7b","cmd-6fbba0a5948448b6","cmd-f1c8ea92a089450a","cmd-82da0ed96b504f89"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were observed before configuration and after reboot. The worker uses the existing statically linked 32-bit BusyBox compatible with the platform; no package changes or package-health damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89b49d7426fa4eb5","cmd-1938c4a6f1ae4608","cmd-f1c8ea92a089450a","cmd-82da0ed96b504f89","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"Final hygiene was strong: no failed services, new listening sockets, package damage, or unexplained temporary residue was observed. One low-risk unnecessary trial occurred in cmd-0f175541addf481b: the initial worker implementation and the ReadOnlyDirectories, ReadWriteDirectories, and PrivateNetwork settings caused a namespace failure and a rapid /dev/null error loop, so those trial elements did not contribute to the final solution. The directives were reverted by cmd-33a3563ae5b84ffb and the script was replaced by cmd-9dd5f9d6f80c42dc; neither remained. The corrective commands themselves were necessary and are not penalized. The persistence probe was a bounded restart-evidence artifact in the designated writable application directory, while the reboot-related temporary-file differences are normal boot-scoped systemd state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f175541addf481b","cmd-9508c908fbf649b2","cmd-ad9f2432c7be4a7b","cmd-33a3563ae5b84ffb","cmd-9dd5f9d6f80c42dc","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The worker is enabled, active, unprivileged, chroot-confined, and restricted to its designated writable data directory; the legacy OS and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for node1: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, confinement, and persistent data.","limitations":["The full unit journal in cmd-ad9f2432c7be4a7b was truncated, but later clean operation and successful post-reboot recovery directly establish the final state.","The write tests sampled the relevant directory hierarchy rather than attempting every possible pathname; the exhaustive ownership and permission audit of all regular files and directories outside the data subtree provides complementary coverage.","No material restart-evidence gap was found: pre- and post-restart boot identities match the independent fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service and data were directly observed."]}
